IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ha-types`
IMPORT `ha-annual`

-- Holidays Act 2003 — GOAL 6: ENFORCEMENT AND RECORDS.
--
--   "Who may enforce the Act; is an employer, or a person involved, liable
--    to a penalty, up to how much, and is the action in time; what may be
--    recovered from a person involved; is the holiday and leave record kept;
--    and is the employment continuous after a dismissal?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2003_129.txt — ss 73-91;
-- Schedule 1AA cls 1-2.

§ `Goal 6 — enforcement and records`

§§ `Who may enforce (s 74)`

-- s 74 "(1) The provisions of this Act may be enforced ... by— (a) an
-- employee: (b) an authorised representative: (c) a representative of a
-- union of which the employee is a member: (d) an employer: (e) a Labour
-- Inspector. (2) An employee's entitlement to annual holidays, public
-- holidays, sick leave, bereavement leave, or family violence leave that are
-- in addition to entitlements under this Act may be enforced only by the
-- persons listed in subsection (1)(a) to (c)."
@ref s 74
GIVEN e IS AN Enforcer, enhanced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may enforce` e `, an entitlement beyond the Act:` enhanced IF
    IF   enhanced
    THEN     e EQUALS `(a) the employee`
          OR e EQUALS `(b) an authorised representative`
          OR e EQUALS `(c) a representative of the employee's union`
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `Penalties (ss 75, 76; Schedule 1AA cl 2)`

-- Schedule 1AA cl 2 "The amendments made by the 2016 Act do not apply to
-- conduct that occurred before the commencement of that Act." The Holidays
-- Amendment Act 2016 came into force on 1 April 2016 (the date is that
-- Act's). It rewrote s 75 and inserted s 77A; the earlier text is not
-- carried.
@ref Schedule 1AA cl 2
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` d IF
    d AT LEAST Date 1 4 2016

`conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 amendments, which this encoding does not carry` MEANS
    REFUSE "conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 amendments, which this encoding does not carry"

-- s 75(2) "The provisions are— section 16 and sections 21 to 28 ...: section
-- 40(3) ...: sections 28A and 28B ...: section 46, sections 49 to 56,
-- section 60, and section 61(3) ...: section 63, section 65, and sections 69
-- to 72 ...: sections 72C and 72H to 72J ...: section 81 ...: section 82".
@ref s 75(2)
GIVEN p IS A `Provision breached`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a provision listed in s 75(2)` p IF
    NOT p EQUALS `another provision`

-- s 75(1) "An employer who fails to comply with any of the provisions listed
-- in subsection (2), and every person who is involved in the failure to
-- comply, is liable,— (a) if the employer or the person ... is an
-- individual, to a penalty not exceeding $10,000: (b) if ... a company or
-- other body corporate, to a penalty not exceeding $20,000." (3) involved
-- means a person involved in a breach under s 142W of the Employment
-- Relations Act 2000 (an input).
@ref s 75; Schedule 1AA cl 2
@export The maximum penalty under s 75 of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ) for an employer's failure to comply with a provision listed in s 75(2), for the employer or a person involved in the failure: $10,000 for an individual and $20,000 for a company or other body corporate; 0 if the provision is not listed or the person neither the employer nor involved. Conduct before 1 April 2016 is refused. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Provision breached`  @desc The provision the employer failed to comply with
      `the employer` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person is the employer
      involved IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person is involved in the failure (ERA s 142W)
      kind IS A `Kind of person`  @desc An individual, or a company or other body corporate
      conduct IS A DATE  @desc The day of the failure to comply
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty under s 75 for a breach of` p `, the employer:` `the employer` `, involved:` involved `, a person who is` kind `, conduct on` conduct MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` conduct
            THEN `conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 amendments, which this encoding does not carry`
        IF `a provision listed in s 75(2)` p AND (`the employer` OR involved)
            THEN CONSIDER kind
                 WHEN `an individual` THEN 10000
                 WHEN `a company or other body corporate` THEN 20000
        OTHERWISE 0

-- s 76 "(1) A Labour Inspector and the employee concerned are the only
-- persons who may bring an action in the Authority against an employer to
-- recover a penalty under section 75. (1A) However, only a Labour Inspector
-- may bring an action ... against a person involved".
@ref s 76(1)-(1A)
GIVEN e IS AN Enforcer, `against the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may bring a penalty action` e `, against the employer:` `against the employer` IF
        e EQUALS `(e) a Labour Inspector`
    OR  (`against the employer` AND e EQUALS `(a) the employee`)

-- s 76(5) "An action for the recovery of a penalty must be commenced within
-- 12 months after the earlier of when the cause of action became known, or
-- should reasonably have become known, to the Labour Inspector or employee
-- concerned." (5A) "Despite subsection (5), if a court refuses to make a
-- pecuniary penalty order under section 142E of the Employment Relations Act
-- 2000, an action ... in relation to the same matter must be commenced
-- within 3 months after the refusal." FORK F6 again: the anniversary (or the
-- day 3 months on) is the last day.
@ref s 76(5)-(5A)
GIVEN known IS A DATE, `should have known` IS A DATE, refusal IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to commence a penalty action, known` known `, should have known` `should have known` `, court refused` refusal MEANS
    CONSIDER refusal
    WHEN JUST r THEN `add months` r 3
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add years` (IF known LESS THAN `should have known` THEN known ELSE `should have known`) 1

§§ `Arrears (ss 77, 77A)`

-- s 77A "(1) A Labour Inspector or an employee may recover from a person who
-- is not the employee's employer any unpaid holiday pay or leave pay that
-- the employee is entitled to if— (a) the employee is entitled to unpaid
-- holiday pay or leave pay under this Act; and (b) the holiday pay or leave
-- pay is unpaid due to non-compliance with this Act; and (c) the person ...
-- is a person involved in the non-compliance. (2) However, ... only,— (a) in
-- the case of recovery by an employee, with the prior leave of the Authority
-- or court; and (b) to the extent that the employee's employer is unable to
-- pay".
@ref s 77A; Schedule 1AA cl 2
@export The unpaid holiday pay or leave pay a Labour Inspector or the employee may recover from a person involved in the employer's non-compliance under s 77A of the Holidays Act 2003 (NZ): only so much as the employer is unable to pay, and for an employee only with the prior leave of the Authority or court. Conduct before 1 April 2016 is refused. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN Enforcer  @desc Who seeks to recover
      involved IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Whether the person is involved in the non-compliance (ERA s 142W)
      leave IS A BOOLEAN  @desc For an employee, whether the Authority or court gave prior leave
      unpaid IS A NUMBER  @desc The holiday pay or leave pay unpaid because of non-compliance with the Act
      `the employer can pay` IS A NUMBER  @desc How much of it the employer is able to pay
      conduct IS A DATE  @desc The day of the non-compliance
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the arrears recoverable under s 77A by` e `, involved:` involved `, leave:` leave `, unpaid` unpaid `, the employer can pay` `the employer can pay` `, conduct on` conduct MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the 2016 amendments apply to conduct on` conduct
            THEN `conduct before 1 April 2016 falls under the Act as it stood before the 2016 amendments, which this encoding does not carry`
        IF     involved
           AND (   e EQUALS `(e) a Labour Inspector`
                OR (e EQUALS `(a) the employee` AND leave))
            THEN max 0 (unpaid MINUS `the employer can pay`)
        OTHERWISE 0

§§ `The holiday and leave record (ss 81-83)`

-- s 81(1)-(2) "An employer must at all times keep a holiday and leave record
-- showing, in the case of each employee ..., the following information" and
-- (3) "must be kept— (a) in written form; or (b) in a form or in a manner
-- that allows the information ... to be easily accessed and converted into
-- written form." Items that apply only "if applicable" are given as TRUE
-- where they do not apply. The last item, "any other particulars that may
-- be prescribed", depends on regulations and is not carried.
@ref s 81(1)-(3)
GIVEN r IS A `Holiday and leave record`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the holiday and leave record meets s 81` r IF
    all (GIVEN b YIELD b)
        (LIST r's `name`, r's `date employment commenced`,
              r's `hours worked each day in a pay period and the pay for them`,
              r's `current entitlement to annual holidays`, r's `date last entitled to annual holidays`,
              r's `current entitlement to sick leave`, r's `dates of annual holidays and leave taken`,
              r's `payment for annual holidays and leave taken`, r's `portion of annual holidays paid out`,
              r's `date and amount of each payout`, r's `dates of, and payments for, public holidays worked`,
              r's `hours worked on public holidays`, r's `public holidays transferred and the days they went to`,
              r's `date of entitlement to each alternative holiday`, r's `public and alternative holidays not worked but paid`,
              r's `cash value of board or lodgings`, r's `payments in exchange for alternative holidays`,
              r's `date of termination`, r's `holiday pay paid on termination`,
              r's `kept in written form, or convertible into it`)

-- s 81(4) "Information entered in the holiday and leave record must be kept
-- for not less than 6 years after the date on which the information is
-- entered."
@ref s 81(4)
GIVEN entered IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first day the information may be discarded, entered` entered MEANS
    `the day` 1 `days after` (`add years` entered 6)

-- s 82(1) "The following persons may request ... (a) the employee: (b) an
-- authorised representative: (c) a representative of a union of which the
-- employee is a member: (d) a Labour Inspector."
@ref s 82(1)
GIVEN e IS AN Enforcer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may request access to the holiday and leave record` e IF
    NOT e EQUALS `(d) an employer`

-- s 83 "(3) If ... the Authority is satisfied that the employer failed to
-- comply with section 81 or section 82 and that the failure prevented the
-- claimant from bringing an accurate claim, the Authority may make a finding
-- to that effect. (4) If a finding under subsection (3) is made, then the
-- Authority may accept as proved, in the absence of evidence to the
-- contrary, statements made by the employee about— (a) holiday pay or leave
-- pay actually paid ...: (b) annual holidays, public holidays, sick leave,
-- bereavement leave, or family violence leave actually taken".
@ref s 83(3)-(4)
GIVEN failed IS A BOOLEAN, prevented IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Authority may accept the employee's statements, failure to comply with s 81 or 82:` failed `, prevented an accurate claim:` prevented IF
    failed AND prevented

§§ `Continuous employment after re-employment (s 85)`

-- s 85 "(1) If an employer dismisses an employee and then re-employs the
-- employee within 1 month after the dismissal, the employee's employment
-- must be treated as being continuous ... (2) Subsection (1) does not apply
-- if a Labour Inspector makes a determination that the Labour Inspector is
-- satisfied that— (a) the employer acted in good faith; and (b) the employer
-- did not act for the purpose of evading his or her obligations".
@ref s 85
GIVEN dismissed IS A DATE, reemployed IS A DATE, determination IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employment is treated as continuous, dismissed` dismissed `, re-employed` reemployed `, Labour Inspector determination under s 85(2):` determination IF
        reemployed AT MOST `add months` dismissed 1
    AND NOT determination

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

-- These provisions confer no entitlement the encoding computes; they are
-- listed so the coverage table can account for them.
@ref ss 1-7, 11, 12, 13, 15, 17, 18(2)-(4), 20, 28C-28D, 28F, 29, 31, 41-43, 46, 51, 54, 58, 62, 64, 72A, 72E, 72G, 73, 76(2)-(4), 76(6), 76A, 76B, 77, 78-80, 81(3A)-(3C), 81(5), 84, 86-91, Schedule 1AA cls 1, 3, 4, Schedules 1-3
`provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 1 title", "s 2 commencement", "s 3 purpose", "s 4 overview", "s 5 interpretation", "s 5A Schedule 1AA",
         "s 6 the Act is a minimum; terms that reduce it have no effect", "s 6A (no text in this version)", "s 7 application; the Armed Forces excluded",
         "s 11 Labour Inspector determines pay measures", "s 12 otherwise a working day (an input)", "s 13 Labour Inspector determines a working day",
         "s 15 purpose", "s 17 how the 4 weeks are met", "s 18(2)-(4) taking annual holidays by agreement", "s 20 holidays in advance",
         "s 28C requirement to request payout prohibited", "s 28D requirement to make payout prohibited", "s 28F Labour Inspector determines payout",
         "s 29 meaning of closedown", "s 31 closedowns by part of business", "ss 41, 42 (no text in this version)", "s 43 purpose",
         "s 46 entitlement to public holidays", "s 51 transitional pay for public holidays (to 2007)", "s 54 Labour Inspector determines public holiday pay",
         "s 58 (no text in this version)", "s 62 purpose", "s 64 notice of sick or bereavement leave", "s 72A purpose", "s 72E notice of family violence leave",
         "s 72G proof of family violence", "s 81(3A)-(3C), (5) usual hours and the wages and time record", "s 73 good faith and information", "s 76(2)-(4), (6) joinder, judgment, payment of penalties",
         "s 76A matters for the penalty", "s 76B enforcing a penalty", "s 77 Labour Inspector proceedings for arrears",
         "ss 78-80 Labour Inspector powers and determinations", "s 84 interest", "s 86 holiday pay is salary or wages",
         "s 87 regulations", "ss 88-90 transitional from the Holidays Act 1981", "s 91 repeals and amendments",
         "Schedule 1AA cls 1, 3, 4", "Schedules 1-3"
